WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.720
Oil. Copper. Cocoa.

2
00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:05.250
Diamonds. The world wants them,

3
00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:08.290
and some countries have
them in huge amounts.

4
00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:13.310
Across the developing world,
95 of 142 countries depend

5
00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:16.940
on commodities like these for
most of the goods they export.

6
00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:18.510
Some have done well.

7
00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:21.200
Botswana grew fast with its diamonds.

8
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.920
Yet resource-rich countries
often grow more slowly.

9
00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:26.960
So why can a country full of oil,

10
00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.830
copper or cocoa still
stay poor for decades?

11
00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:33.280
In this mission, you'll
draw the cycle that can

12
00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:35.330
keep a poor country poor.

13
00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:38.650
Then you'll shift demand in
a commodity market yourself,

14
00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:40.480
and watch what the price does.

15
00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:44.360
Your mission: find out what
really holds these countries back.
